id: pm-ez1dfg
title: "Half of the pm events payload is per-row resume cursors an agent never reads: 48 percent of stream bytes buy a capability consumed once per batch"
description: "Measured 2026-07-26 on the shipped build: 33,667 of 69,766 bytes over 200 events (48 percent), 1,710 of 3,204 over 10 events (53 percent), are opaque base64 cursors whose decoded fields are either batch-constant (version, fingerprint) or already plaintext in the row (ts, stream_id). A resuming consumer needs only the last cursor. Duplicate check 2026-07-26: searched events/cursor/NDJSON/token-cost items across all statuses; pm-e200 (closed) built the stream, pm-kvxqp1 is the general encoding study, pm-5t33or declares budgets, pm-t5dt4z reports spend. No item covers this stream's per-row cursor redundancy."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[7]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:sdk",context-management,output-contract,scale,token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-07-26T05:42:49.365Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-17T08:52:34.303Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-17T07:37:18.454Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-17T07:37:18.454Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "The default pm events emission carries the resume cursor once per batch rather than once per row, preserving exact resumability with at most one batch of idempotent replay after a consumer crash; the previous per-row shape stays available behind an explicit opt-in flag for consumers that commit per row; already-issued cursors remain accepted by --since indefinitely, pinned by a test that replays a literal old-form cursor; --follow emits a cursor at each batch boundary and uses that boundary as an idle heartbeat; the per-fact token cost of each shape is measured, declared as a budget, and gated so the ratio cannot regress; the batch-boundary definition agrees with the row-streaming contract in pm-mav1ak rather than introducing a second notion of a batch"
goal: project management = context management
objective: Resume capability is paid for once per batch instead of once per fact
value: "The fleet-coordination primitive stops charging roughly 8,400 tokens per 200 events for data no consumer reads; the saving scales with exactly the agent count the scale milestone targets"
why_now: "pm events is the surface a thousand-agent fleet and the planned derived read index both poll continuously, so its per-row overhead is multiplied by the factor the scale work is trying to make affordable"
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: "Default event pages and follow batches carry one terminal resume cursor; --cursor-mode row preserves per-row checkpoints; SDK, CLI, MCP, tool schema, contracts, and docs are aligned."
expected_result: Resume capability is paid once per batch without losing historical-cursor or per-row compatibility.
actual_result: "Batch framing, row opt-in, literal legacy cursor replay, idle heartbeat boundaries, and a <=0.60 batch-to-row byte ratio are covered and green."
